# Allow-list: the image build sees only what the Dockerfile builds from.
# Everything else in the project — notes, backup/ with its source tarballs (each
# carrying the real .env), compose files, docs, CI, screenshots — stays out, and
# anything added to the project later stays out too until it is listed here.
# The finished image takes nothing from this context but the compiled binary.
*

# Backend stage: go build, which embeds the offline recovery tool.
!go.mod
!go.sum
!main.go
!embed_recover.go
!internal/
!scripts/dockback-recover.py

# Frontend stage: npm ci && npm run build.
!frontend/

# Inside what is allowed: rebuilt in the image anyway, or only read by tests.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
internal/web/dist/
**/*_test.go
frontend/src/**/*.test.ts
frontend/src/**/*.test.tsx

# Secrets and local data never belong in a build, even inside allowed folders.
**/.env*
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite*
**/*.key
**/*.pem
